WEBVTT

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.790
Twansform!

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:07.500
Bam!

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.170
Bam!

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.250
Seita, you like that, huh?

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.330
I like it!

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.580
Twansform!

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.380
<b>30 minutes</b>

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.380
<b>later</b>

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:19.880
Transform!

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.420
Twansform!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.920
<b>2 hours</b>

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.920
<b>later</b>

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:23.420
Transform!

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.080
Twansform!

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.420
Mom, what's for dinner?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.420
Transform!

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.920
Twansform!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:30.960
What's wrong?

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.500
He doesn't get bored doing
the same thing over and over?

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.830
Twansform!

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.460
Ah, you used to do similar things a lot too.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.380
Adios!

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.920
<b>Settings</b>

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.920
<b>Restart</b>

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.330
Mamma! Again!

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.920
<b>Chapters</b>

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.750
That's enough, Seita. You've watched too much TV.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.380
No kidding.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.080
I've watched this way too many times,
and now I know the transformation scene by heart.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.250
Mamma! Again, again!

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.630
Hey, Junta.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.250
Would you take Seita outside to play?

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.580
Aww!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.170
If you do, tonight we'll have hamburger steak.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.580
All right.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.380
Twansform!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.130
Twansform!

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.460
Twansform!

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:11.750
Twansform!

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.830
Even though we're outside, he's still at it.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.210
Twansform!

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.790
He doesn't quite have it down though.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.630
Twansform!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.920
There's no one else around right now.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.670
Twansform!

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.380
Seita, Seita. Watch this.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:34.960
Transform!

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.500
Cool!

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.880
That's how to transform. Got it?

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.750
Big bwutha's cool!

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.830
Again!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.630
No point fighting it.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:58.750
Transform!

00:01:59.040 --> 00:01:59.830
Twansform!

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.040
Great job!

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.540
Transform!

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.630
Twansform!

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.540
Transform!

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:09.630
Twansform!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.380
Oh, sorry, don't mind me. As you were.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.130
Big bwutha, one more time!

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.380
One more time.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:23.380
Not doing it.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.330
Transform!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.380
Twansform!

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:27.790
Transform!

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.210
<b>Episode 4: Red Heart and Secret Admirer</b>

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.710
I guess I was half asleep this morning,

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.250
because I accidently put on socks
that aren't the same length.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.790
Second period was gym class, but no one batted an eye.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.580
Well, that's normal for me.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.040
It's almost Valentine's Day.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.920
I can't wait!

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.790
Tama, why do you always get sweets,
but never give any?

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.170
Kubocchi's giving me some too!

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.710
Hmm, shall I?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.830
Huh, you're not getting me anything?

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.670
It seems unlikely that someone like Kubo-san
would make the sort of mistakes I make.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.630
Kubo-san seems kinda off today.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.000
What's wrong?

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:47.830
Huh?

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.250
Weren't you staring at me just now?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.330
She caught me red-handed.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.830
No, it's nothing.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.580
Really?

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.580
And for that reason, I'm giving a lot of homework today.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.580
Everyone, make sure to do a good job!

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.460
But really...

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.750
She does seem different than usual.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.080
What exactly is going on with her?

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.920
While I puzzled over that, school let out.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.790
Kubo, can you please put up the new printouts?

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:26.960
Yes, sir!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.830
I made it through the day without
anyone noticing my socks.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.830
Shiraishi-kun, give me a hand.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.540
Huh? Oh, sure.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.830
<b>Let's take precautions against spreading infections</b>

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.290
I just barely can't reach it.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.380
Shiraishi-kun, can you do it?

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.830
But I'm not much taller than her.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.500
Yeah, sure.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.880
<b>Let's take precautions against spreading infections</b>

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:58.500
But if I tiptoe, I should be able to reach it.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.750
If she sees my socks...

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.830
She'll definitely mess with me!

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.790
Looks like I can't reach it either.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.040
I'll get a chair.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.000
You don't need to be feel so self-conscious about it.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:16.380
About what?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.830
Your socks.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.380
Sh-she noticed!

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.380
Eh?

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.750
Doesn't the printout look crooked?

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.630
No, it's not. Probably.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.330
Really?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.420
Maybe what caused that off vibe this morning was her...

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:45.750
Tights?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.790
Oh, crap!

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:57.040
Shiraishi-kun, you noticed I'm wearing tights today.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.540
Uh, yeah.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.170
My socks weren't dry today, so I wore tights.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:09.540
You wouldn't think it, but it takes so long for socks to dry.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.880
No teasing... Is she sick?

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.210
So, Shiraishi-kun...

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.290
You were staring at my legs.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.380
Dirty boy.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.130
No, that's not, I... it's not that
I was staring at them just now.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.080
I felt like something was different about you all day.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.960
Hmm, gotcha.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.080
You stared all day, huh?

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.040
Er, um...

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:40.460
Shiraishi-kun.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:44.210
Shall we continue putting up the printouts?

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:46.830
Yeah.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Oh, yeah.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:57.790
Shiraishi-kun, have you ever had one of those
convenience store drinks you get a cup for?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:58.170
<b>Let's take precautions against spreading infections</b>

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:58.170
<b>Common cold</b>

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:58.170
<b>Influenza</b>

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.580
A cup?

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.290
Like for coffee or hot chocolate.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.880
Um... You get the cup at
the counter and fill it up yourself.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:05.960
Oh.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.250
Those.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.210
Yeah, I have. Why do you ask?

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.170
Shiraishi-kun.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.210
Let's go home together!

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:20.710
Huh?

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.000
I've been wanting to try that type of drink!

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.250
That's fine with me.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.540
Awesome!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.670
They're not, like, amazing or anything though.

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.290
There are so many choices!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.170
Yep.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.380
What should I choose?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.540
Hot chocolate, matcha latte... Hmm!

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.250
She's having a tough time deciding. If I was with Seita...

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.630
All right, how about we get two drinks
and each drink half of one.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.130
Yeah! Half!

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.040
Then we could just do that.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.920
What are you getting?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.380
I'm thinking a warm drink would hit the spot.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.330
I dunno. Honestly, any of them would be good.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.000
Then...

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:12.130
How about you get a hot chocolate,
and I get a matcha latte?

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.210
Huh?

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:16.130
And then we both can drink half of each drink?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.960
She's totally toying with me.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.580
I don't really want a drink. I'll get a meat bun.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.630
That's too bad. Well, I'll get a matcha latte then.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:32.330
So you only need to ask them for
a matcha latte. I'll get my meat b-

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.630
Um, Kubo-san?

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:39.540
Come with me.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:47.250
You're invisible, so if anything happens,
you'll swoop in and save me like a guardian angel.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:50.290
Just who the heck do you think I am?

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.920
I'll have a matcha latte, please.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.210
What size would you like?

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:55.920
Huh?

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.170
Kubo-san didn't realize there are different sizes.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:07.210
She's summoning her guardian angel.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.670
Their sizes are regular and large.
A regular is basically a medium.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.210
Thank you, guardian angel.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.630
A regular, please! Oh, and
I'll also have a meat bun, please!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.080
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.420
Nice, he didn't notice you!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.130
He sure didn't.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:37.830
Kubo-san?

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.920
Y-you just gotta press this button, right?

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.580
She's beaming.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.170
That's right.

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.420
Oh, put down the cup first!

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:48.420
Oh, okay.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.630
<b>Repeat</b>

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.630
<b>Please take your cup</b>

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.630
Is it done?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.380
Yep.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:07.130
<b>Matcha</b>

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:07.130
<b>Latte</b>

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.540
Mission accomplished!

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:12.920
It's amazing!

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.330
She actually had never bought one before.

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.130
That's surprising. She seems like the type
of person who can do anything.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.460
You want some? It's really good!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.670
Nah, I'm good.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:24.880
Really?

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.210
I've got my meat bun.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.170
I'm not falling for her trap.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.960
Hey, lemme try your meat bun.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.290
My meat bun?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.210
In that case, I'll just tear off a piece and give it to her.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.830
That's cool with me. I'll just tear off a-

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.210
Oh, no need for that.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.380
I'll just take a bite.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.500
Hmm, that's tasty. Thanks.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:58.170
Shiraishi-kun, aren't you gonna eat?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:01.420
You should eat it while it's still warm.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.960
Well, I gotta go this way. Thanks for today.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.380
Oh, sure.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.210
Welp, see you tomorrow!

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.670
See you tomorrow.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.960
It's my meat bun, after all.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.580
Huh? Did we bump into something?

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.420
Eh? Was it just our imagination?

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.960
<b>Warm</b>

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.960
<b>Latte</b>

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.630
<b>February</b>

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.630
<b>National Foundation Day</b>

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:51.630
<b>Valentine's Day</b>

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:51.630
<b>The Emperor's Birthday</b>

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:55.250
<b>Valentine's Day</b>

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.580
Valentine's Day.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.580
The day that girls gift boys chocolate,

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:02.380
and sometimes, even confess their love.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.330
At first glance, this seems like an event for girls.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.080
Nay! Valentine's Day is a festival for boys!

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:12.670
And, naturally, the entry ticket
for this festival is chocolate!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:17.000
In order to receive chocolate, some boys
butter up the girls with kindness.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.000
I'll carry that for you.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.080
Thank you!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.750
Some freak out.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:24.080
Some pray to god.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.750
And some never had a chance to begin with.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:34.130
It's Valentine's Day, huh?
I thought everyone seemed on edge today.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:38.290
For me, Valentine's Day is just another ordinary day.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:44.580
In elementary school, the teacher said
she'd pass out chocolate to all the students, but...

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.670
I'm passing out chocolate to everyone!

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:53.540
Teachers have a track record of forgetting I exist
and not passing things back to me.

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:54.210
<b>Crinkle</b>

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.920
Other people usually do a quintuple
take when they see me,

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:33.750
but now I'm the one doing a quintuple take!

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.630
Someone forgot their sweets in my desk!

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:39.420
<b>Junta Shiraishi, age 16, doesn't think this treat is for him.</b>

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.880
Of all the desks to leave this in...

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.330
Or maybe they thought this was someone else's desk.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:49.170
Or could there possibly be someone
who would give me obligation chocolate?

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.040
The person I usually talk to is...

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.420
K..Kubo-san.

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:57.250
Fat chance of that!

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:59.170
Ah, you scared me!

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.750
Does your forehead hurt?

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.250
It's red.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.040
Woosh!

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.420
How long has she been there?

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.130
Huh?

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.540
Tiptoe.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:16.750
Oh, he came back.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:21.670
That's it. Why don't I just ask her?

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.750
"Did you get me this?" It's only a few words.

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.790
Kubo-san...

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:35.380
Um...

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.880
Nice weather today, huh?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.920
Yeah, it really is.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.580
Well, I don't really need to ask her.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.920
There's no way I was given chocolate anyway.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:57.920
But it's possible someone actually left theirs in my desk,
so for now, I'll just leave it be.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.130
Shiraishi-kun.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.920
Today's Valentine's Day.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:05.670
Yeah.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:10.830
Has someone ever given you
chocolate on Valentine's Day?

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:12.330
Nope.

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:13.580
Oh, really.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:18.630
I see.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.250
Kubo-san seems oddly pleased.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:24.960
Is she...

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.500
Oh, that's right.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.920
I think someone put sweets in your desk.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.630
Kubo-san, do you know something about this?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:34.250
Yep.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.960
She put a ton of effort into making them.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:41.580
So...

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.420
Be sure to enjoy them.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.750
I can't help but think they're not actually for me though.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:53.580
Oh, they're for you, all right. I'll leave it at that.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.880
Wh-what, Kubo-san?

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:00.790
And she's gone.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:05.130
So who are they from?

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:11.500
Who indeed?

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.330
I'm not saying a word.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:20.130
I'm home!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.920
Nagisa, what's up with those big bags?

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:30.580
Tomorrow's Valentine's Day. I'm gonna make sweets.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:35.580
Oh, yeah, it is! I'm getting nostalgic. Ah, Valentine's Day!

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.670
Wait. You're making them?

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:36.710
<b>Huh</b>

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Chocolate Nuts</b>

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Family Pack</b>

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Thunder</b>

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Chocolate</b>

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Chocolate</b>

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.000
<b>Victory Ma'am</b>

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.790
The same girl who buys assorted
chocolates and cookies every year,

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:42.880
tosses them in a bag, and calls it a day?

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:48.040
The same girl who has even burned pancakes?

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:52.750
The same girl who doesn't know the
difference between lettuce and cabbage...

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:53.830
Is going to bake?

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.830
Akina, just shut it.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.170
<b>Put chopped chocolate (100 g) into a bowl, and</b>

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.170
<b>then heat it in a 600-watt microwave for 1.5</b>

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.170
<b>minutes so the chocolate melts.</b>

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.580
<b>2. Mix flour</b>

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.580
<b>First, sift in flour, then mix with a rubber spatula</b>

00:17:58.590 --> 00:17:59.580
<b>(no kneading required).</b>

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:01.540
Um, so next is...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.290
That same girl...

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:12.330
And done!

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.920
Oh, lemme see!

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.920
What is this dark matter?

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.290
It doesn't matter as long as it tastes good.

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:24.080
That's an extreme position.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:32.540
Nagisa, I advise you not to give these to anyone.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.920
You should give them store-bought
stuff like you usually do.

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:47.790
No. I'm trying again.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:52.750
Is there someone you want to give
homemade sweets to that badly?

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.500
Oh, my.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:59.750
I'm only giving sweets to my friends.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.210
She's so easy to read... It's written all over her face.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.830
Well, maybe I'll bake some sweets too.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.500
I don't want any help.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.630
But I'm only going to be making a treat for myself.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.540
Maybe I'll make some cookies.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.460
That's what I'm making.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.920
Oh, are you?

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:27.630
<b>Moon</b>

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:27.630
<b>Flour</b>

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:27.630
<b>Aomori Butter</b>

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:27.540
To bake cookies, it's important to
precisely measure your ingredients.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.670
Um, first you whip the butter
into a cream-like consistency.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.830
How about we make our sweets together?

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:38.540
If you watch me and follow along,
I think you'll do a great job.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.920
I am a genius, after all.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.170
Akina...

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.170
Can you pass the butter?

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.330
Here you go.

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.210
Done!

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:04.750
Sure enough, I'm a genius! I'm brilliant!

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.040
Mine's a little deformed.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.040
Mmm. Huh.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.290
Even though we made the same thing...

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:28.880
Your cookies taste better because
you put lots of love into them.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:34.750
Anyone would be delighted to get
something you worked so hard to make.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:39.170
Besides, not all of them are weirdly shaped.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:42.750
Look, the cookie in the middle is super aesthetic.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.080
All right. Now I'm all ready for Valentine's Day tomorrow!

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:26.250
Akina, thanks for earlier.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.250
Hmm? But I didn't do anything.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:30.670
That's not-

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:31.290
Heh.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:32.920
Eh...

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:42.500
I hate this about you!

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:45.880
I love seeing you look so cute!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:53.130
By the way, who are you giving
the best-looking cookie to?

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.170
That's...

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.130
My personal business.

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.750
Who gave this to me?

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:10.130
It's great.
